<BaseLayout title="What is UXO?" description="A plain-language introduction to unexploded ordnance.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Foundations</p><h1>What is unexploded ordnance?</h1><p class="lead">UXO is explosive ordnance that has been fired, dropped, launched, or otherwise deployed but did not function as intended and remains hazardous.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><h2>One part of a wider problem.</h2></div><div class="copy"><dl class="term-list"><div><dt>UXO</dt><dd>Explosive ordnance that was used or prepared for use but did not explode as intended.</dd></div><div><dt>AXO</dt><dd>Abandoned explosive ordnance: items left behind or dumped and no longer under the control of the party that left them.</dd></div><div><dt>ERW</dt><dd>Explosive remnants of war, a term used in international law primarily for UXO and AXO.</dd></div><div><dt>EO</dt><dd>Explosive ordnance, a broader mine-action term that can include mines, cluster munitions, UXO, AXO, booby traps, and other explosive devices.</dd></div></dl><p>These categories overlap in public discussion but are not interchangeable. UXO.INFO uses the terms as precisely as the available source allows.</p><p>Whatever the category, do not touch, move, investigate, or attempt to make an item safe. Leave the area when possible and report it through appropriate local channels.</p><p class="notice">This site provides general awareness information only. Follow local authority and specialist advice in an actual situation.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section section--quiet"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Read further</p><h2>Use primary references.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>The ICRC explains UXO and other explosive remnants of war in plain language, while the legal framework for recording, warnings, risk education, marking, and clearance is set out in Protocol V to the Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons.</p><a class="action-link" href="/resources">Sources &amp; resources</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
